  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A limited ed. artist's book of 30 copies, numbered and signed by Maureen Cummins and Nicole Cooley.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">" ... [P]rinted and produced by Maureen Cummins ... The project is a collaboration between Cummins and the poet Nicole Cooley, based on research done at the American Antiquarian Society. The cycle of poems was created by Cooley specifically for this book; the accompanying images are from a penmanship book kept by a Salem boy, Josiah Peele, during the years 1808 and 1809. Salem Lessons was printed with offset, letterpress and silkscreen technologies on Johannot paper. The end pages are a handmade sheet, Belgique, created by HMP."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Accordion-folded pages with slate covers; issued in a black cloth-covered four-flap enclosure case with black tape ties.</subfield>
